WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:08.269
Speaker 1: The Republican National Committee
is now joining Donald Trump and others in

00:00:08.269 --> 00:00:15.730
desperately trying to keep their own email
records away from the Jan. six committee investigating

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.140
the Trump riots of 2021.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.730
Once again, this is not the behavior of parties
who have nothing to hide.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.230
CNN report.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:32.320
RNC tries to stop 2020 email communications
data from going to the January 6th Committee

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.450
on Wednesday.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:39.040
The House Select Committee investigating the
attack on the U.S. Capitol is poised to receive

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.330
data from the Republican Party's email communications
platform.

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:48.430
Salesforce, and the Republican National Committee
rushed to court last night to try to block

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:49.460
it.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:53.820
The development is the latest to emerge about
the house's aggressive pursuits reconstructing

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:59.370
political misinformation after the 2020 election
that contributed to Trump supporters storming

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.720
the Capitol on January 6th.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:07.079
The RNC alleges that the House subpoenaed
a salesforce seeking information about election

00:01:07.079 --> 00:01:10.070
communications, including those related to
former President Trump.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:17.670
Quote would give the select committee unprecedented
access to the RNC's internal political strategies

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:24.530
and to private personal information regarding
supporters, practically adding reasons that

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:27.429
their emails should be investigated.

00:01:27.429 --> 00:01:35.200
What were they telling their big donors right
on the eve of the January 6th Trump riots,

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.750
political strategies which they want to hide
are exactly what got these people where they

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:40.759
are now.

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:45.420
Political strategies that involve lying about
election results, intimidation, calling for

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.920
violence, spreading fear and propaganda through
right wing media, trying to invalidate voters,

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:55.319
purge voter rolls, change vote totals send
AlterNet bogus slates of electors.

00:01:55.319 --> 00:01:58.389
All of those things are why we're in this
mess.

00:01:58.389 --> 00:02:04.039
And so the January 6th committee is 100 percent
right to say, hey, maybe they were talking

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:09.979
about that stuff in their email communications,
and if there isn't illegal stuff in there,

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:11.760
they don't really have anything to worry about.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.570
I mean, everybody knows what the strategies
are.

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:18.030
You think we're going to learn about new strategies
by looking at their emails?

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.640
We know what the strategies are.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:23.980
What we might learn is that they were openly
plotting and communicating about them with

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.040
donors and other higher ups.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.090
The article goes on.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:32.190
Last week, the RNC filed a lawsuit against
the House Committee complaining about the

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:35.400
Salesforce Salesforce subpoenas breath.

